It would be wholly unrealistic to expect of a person under assault, to modulate his defence step by step according to the attack;
Fourthly, the right extends to the killing of the actual or potential assailant when there is] a reasonable and imminent apprehension of the atrocious crimes enumerated in the six clauses .
